+//! Cleanup-edge removal (Stage 3b): the O group's pass that turns a protected operation's
+//! [`RTerm::Invoke`] into a [`RTerm::Goto`] where its cleanup edge provably cannot matter.
+//!
+//! Every `Unwind::Cleanup` of a release build becomes an `Invoke` (`lower/ssa.rs`), printed as a
+//! `try { op; $invokeN = 1 } catch ($caught) { if (__rt.is_abort($caught)) throw $caught; ... }`
+//! (`lower/js/emit.rs`), and a function holding one is closed to inlining, partial escape
+//! analysis, and fusion. An edge goes when one of two proofs holds:
+//!
+//! * **EmptyChain** -- structural, no summaries. Every path from the unwind edge reaches the
+//!   rethrow (`Throw(None)`) through operations nothing observes ([`unobservable`]): no store, no
+//!   drop, no call, no assert, no protected operation, no other exit. Running the chain or not is
+//!   indistinguishable: the exception in flight is rethrown either way, with its identity. A
+//!   `Switch` on an unwind-edge argument the edge passes as a constant takes its one arm, which is
+//!   what tells apart two edges sharing a chain of drop-flag tests.
+//! * **NoThrow** -- the protected operation cannot raise a JavaScript exception other than a
+//!   registered abort ([`crate::analysis::effects::Summary::may_throw`] and its per-op transfer).
+//!   The handler rethrows an abort before it runs anything, so the catch could never enter the
+//!   chain. A host call never qualifies unless `js-cleanup-trust-host-contract=on` takes its
+//!   `#[js_extern]` declaration at its word, and then it reports `no-throw-host-contract`.
+//!   A removal only the Stage 4'a proofs make ([`Rules`]: a `Callee::Foreign` call resolved to
+//!   its definition, an audited intrinsic, a closure-creation marker or a drop-free `try`)
+//!   reports which of them it needed: `no-throw-foreign-resolved`, `no-throw-intrinsic`,
+//!   `no-throw-marker`, or `no-throw-combined` for more than one (`removed_new_classes` counts
+//!   each class it needed). The attribution re-derives `may_throw` under [`Rules::STAGE_3B`]
+//!   ([`Summaries::under_rules`]) and never decides an edge. Both rule sets read the
+//!   `HostOperation::may_throw` table as it stands, so an operation only that table makes quiet
+//!   -- the byte export `u8arrayfrombytes`, newly quiet since this pass delegates to the table --
+//!   is reported as a plain `no-throw` and not counted in `removed_new_classes`.
+//!
+//! The classifier runs once, after the effects fixpoint converged, and removing an edge in one
+//! body never changes another body's summary (the chain it orphans is deleted, which only
+//! shrinks what the body does). Each rewritten body is verified and witness-checked
+//! ([`Witness::CleanupEdge`]); a failure restores the protected body and counts
+//! `cleanup.verify-failed`.
+//!
+//! What de-protection changes: an engine `RangeError` (stack overflow, out of memory) inside a
+//! callee proven to run only Rust no longer runs the caller's destructors on its way out. Rust
+//! aborts in both situations; CONTRACT.md records it.
+
+use std::collections::{BTreeMap, BTreeSet};
+use std::fmt::Write as _;
+
+use crate::analysis::callgraph::Callgraph;
+use crate::analysis::effects::{Rules, Summaries, ThrowCause, ThrowFacts};
+use crate::item::JsName;
